{"id":"badac215-df51-54ee-b5de-59f1a71045f8","reference":"JP-1063","title":"Exterior repaint, front elevation","job_type":"exterior_repaint","status":"to_do","scheduled_start":"2026-11-15","site_address":{"line1":"6 North Street","line2":null,"town":"Bristol","county":"City of Bristol","postcode":"BS3 1AB"},"checklist_total":14,"checklist_dealt_with":0,"notes":"Front elevation only, two storeys plus the bay. Access to the front is from the drive; the customer's car must be moved before 8am (she will text when it is done). Park the van on the road, not the drive. Scaffold tower is already on site, locked to the side gate. Render is sound on the left of the bay but has hairline cracks above the first floor windows: rake out and fill with flexible filler before the stabilising coat. There is algae along the base of the wall by the downpipe, so treat it and leave overnight before painting. Colour is Masonry Cream, six tins are in the garage (the side door is open, the key safe code is the same as for the front). Do not paint the stone window surrounds or the lintel over the front door: they are to be left natural. The bay window frames and the front door are to be rubbed down and finished in satin black; the door furniture comes off and goes back on at the end, so keep it in the labelled bag. Please protect the rose bed under the bay with dust sheets and stand ladders on boards, not on the soil. The neighbour at number 14 has asked that nothing is sprayed because of their washing line; brush and roller only. Forecast is dry until Thursday but check before starting each morning, and do not apply masonry paint if rain is due within four hours. Take before photos of every elevation first, including the cracks, and photograph the algae treated area and the finished bay. Customer pays by link after the manager has reviewed the report, so please do not take payment or discuss prices on site.","contact":{"name":"Helen & David Marsh","phone":"07700 900211"},"checklist":[{"id":"